     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered it. You've confirmed the dose, but you haven't given a clinical reason for it, and I can't find one. 50 mg is five times the 10 mg maximum. It's also in the range where overdose toxicity is reported, including profound hypotension and shock that can last a long time because amlodipine has a half-life of 30 to 50 hours. A single order at this dose could seriously harm the patient before anyone could reverse it.\n\nHere are some options:\n\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** Give me 5 mg or 10 mg once daily and I'll enter it right away. If the blood pressure is still uncontrolled, you can add a second agent from another class, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, thiazide, or beta-blocker.\n- **Get a pharmacist or attending to review the dose.** If there's an unusual reason for 50 mg that I don't know about, they can approve it through your hospital's high-alert or override process.\n- **Check for a transcription error.** The intended dose may have been 5 mg.\n\nI can enter the order as soon as you pick one of these."
      }
     ],
